+# Threshold Feature Implementation
+
+This document describes the implementation of the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` command and the corresponding changes to frai-core.
+
+## Overview
+
+The threshold feature allows CI pipelines to fail when evaluation metrics fall below specified minimums. This enables gating model deployments on evaluation quality metrics.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. frai-core/src/eval/index.js
+
+#### `generateReport` function
+- Added optional `thresholds` parameter (object mapping metric IDs to minimum values)
+- Processes thresholds by matching against evaluations
+- Adds to report:
+  - `passed` (boolean): true if all thresholds pass
+  - `thresholds` (array): list of threshold results with structure:
+    ```js
+    {
+      metric: string,      // metric ID
+      min: number,         // minimum required value
+      score: number|null,  // actual metric score (null if metric not found)
+      passed: boolean      // score !== null && score >= min
+    }
+    ```
+- Backward compatible: without thresholds, report is unchanged
+- Handles custom metrics: SDK users can pass any metric ID, it will fail if not found in evaluations
+
+### 2. frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js
+
+#### `toMarkdown` function
+- Added "Thresholds" section to markdown output when thresholds are present
+- Each threshold shows: metric ID, PASS/FAIL status, min value, and actual score
+- Example:
+  ```
+  ## Thresholds
+
+  - **exact_match:** PASS (min: 0.9, score: 0.95)
+  - **toxicity:** FAIL (min: 0.9, score: 0.5)
+  - **custom_metric:** FAIL (min: 0.8, score: n/a)
+  ```
+
+### 3. frai-cli/src/index.ts
+
+#### EvalOptions interface
+- Added `threshold?: string[]` field to support multiple threshold options
+
+#### parseAndValidateThresholds function
+- Validates threshold format: `<metric>=<number>`
+- Validates value is between 0 and 1
+- Validates metric ID is in valid list: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`
+- Returns structured result with validation errors
+- Errors list valid metrics for unknown metric IDs
+
+#### runEvalCommand function
+- Calls `parseAndValidateThresholds` and exits with code 2 if invalid
+- Passes validated thresholds to `generateReport`
+- Writes report before checking threshold results (always outputs report)
+- Exits with code 1 if `report.passed === false`
+- Exits with code 0 if no thresholds or all thresholds pass
+
+#### eval command definition
+- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option with custom accumulator function
+- Option can be used multiple times: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`
+- Description includes example usage
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### CLI Usage
+
+```bash
+# Single threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --threshold toxicity=0.95
+
+# With markdown report
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --format markdown
+
+# Exit code handling in CI
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+if [ $? -eq 1 ]; then
+  echo "Evaluation failed thresholds"
+  exit 1
+fi
+```
+
+### SDK Usage
+
+```typescript
+import { generateReport, runEvaluations } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = runEvaluations({
+  outputs: myOutputs,
+  references: myReferences,
+  metrics: [customMetric]  // can include custom metrics
+});
+
+const report = generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'refs.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    custom_metric: 0.8
+  }
+});
+
+console.log(report.passed);  // true/false
+console.log(report.thresholds);  // detailed results per threshold
+```
+
+## Exit Codes
+
+- **0**: Success (all thresholds pass or no thresholds specified)
+- **1**: Threshold failure (one or more thresholds failed)
+- **2**: Usage error (malformed threshold, invalid value, or unknown metric)
+
+## Report Structure
+
+### JSON Report with Thresholds
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": {
+    "generatedAt": "2024-01-01T12:00:00.000Z",
+    "outputsPath": "/path/to/outputs.json",
+    "referencesPath": "/path/to/refs.json",
+    "totalSamples": 100
+  },
+  "metrics": [
+    {
+      "id": "exact_match",
+      "label": "Exact Match",
+      "score": 0.95,
+      "total": 100,
+      "matches": 95
+    }
+  ],
+  "passed": true,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": 0.95,
+      "passed": true
+    },
+    {
+      "metric": "toxicity",
+      "min": 0.95,
+      "score": 1.0,
+      "passed": true
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### JSON Report without Thresholds
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [ ... ]
+  // No 'passed' or 'thresholds' fields
+}
+```
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+- Without `--threshold` option, CLI behavior is unchanged
+- `generateReport` without thresholds parameter works as before
+- Reports without thresholds have no `passed` or `thresholds` fields
+- All existing code continues to work
+
+## Feature Completeness
+
+✓ Threshold parsing and validation
+✓ CLI --threshold option (repeatable)
+✓ Exit codes (0, 1, 2)
+✓ Report generation with threshold results
+✓ JSON report format with threshold data
+✓ Markdown report with Thresholds section
+✓ Error messages listing valid metrics
+✓ Handling metrics with null scores
+✓ SDK integration (generateReport accepts thresholds)
+✓ Custom metric support
+✓ Documentation (README, design notes)
+✓ Backward compatibility
+
+## Files Modified
+
+1. `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js` - Added threshold logic to generateReport
+2. `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js` - Added Thresholds section to markdown
+3. `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` - Added --threshold option and validation
+4. `/README.md` - Added --threshold documentation
+5. `/docs/eval_harness_design.md` - Added threshold validation section
