+## Threshold Validation
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object mapping metric IDs to minimum acceptable scores (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`).
+- Thresholds are validated per-metric: a metric with `null` score fails its threshold rather than crashing.
+- The report gains a `passed` boolean (true if all thresholds pass) and a `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries for each threshold.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL per threshold.
+- CLI `--threshold <metric=<min>>` option can be used multiple times; invalid format or value exits with code 2 (usage error); threshold failure exits with code 1.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
