+# Threshold Feature Implementation Test
+
+## Feature Summary
+Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option to `frai eval` command and threshold support to `generateReport` in frai-core.
+
+## Implementation Checklist
+
+### Core Logic (frai-core/src/eval/index.js)
+- [x] `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` parameter
+- [x] `generateReport` validates each threshold against evaluations
+- [x] Metric with null score fails its threshold (doesn't crash)
+- [x] Report includes `passed` boolean (true if all thresholds pass)
+- [x] Report includes `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` per threshold
+- [x] Without thresholds parameter, report is unchanged (backward compatible)
+
+### Reporters (frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js)
+- [x] JSON reports include threshold data (unchanged - just serializes report)
+- [x] Markdown reports include "Thresholds" section
+- [x] Markdown shows PASS/FAIL per threshold
+- [x] Markdown shows min value, actual score, and metric name
+
+### CLI (frai-cli/src/index.ts)
+- [x] EvalOptions interface includes `threshold?: string[]`
+- [x] `--threshold` option added to eval command (supports multiple uses)
+- [x] `parseAndValidateThresholds` function validates format `<metric>=<number>`
+- [x] Validates metric is in valid list: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`
+- [x] Validates value is between 0 and 1
+- [x] Exits with code 2 on format/value error with helpful message
+- [x] Lists valid metric ids in error message for unknown metric
+- [x] `runEvalCommand` passes thresholds to `generateReport`
+- [x] Exits with code 1 if `report.passed === false`
+- [x] Report is written either way (whether thresholds pass or fail)
+- [x] Without `--threshold`, behavior is unchanged (exit code always 0)
+
+### Documentation
+- [x] README.md updated with `--threshold` option documentation
+- [x] eval_harness_design.md updated with threshold validation section
+- [x] Documented exit codes (0: success, 1: threshold failure, 2: usage error)
+- [x] Documented valid metric ids
+- [x] Documented min value range (0-1)
+- [x] Documented that threshold can be used multiple times
+
+## Test Cases
+
+### Test 1: Threshold Passes
+**Input:** outputs=["hello","world"], refs=["hello","world"], threshold=exact_match=0.5
+**Expected:** report.passed=true, exact_match threshold shows PASS with score 1.0
+
+### Test 2: Threshold Fails
+**Input:** outputs=["hello","goodbye"], refs=["hello","world"], threshold=exact_match=0.9
+**Expected:** report.passed=false, exact_match threshold shows FAIL with score 0.5
+
+### Test 3: Metric Without Score Fails Threshold
+**Input:** outputs=["hello"], refs=[], threshold=exact_match=0.5
+**Expected:** report.passed=false, threshold shows FAIL with score=null
+
+### Test 4: Multiple Thresholds (Mixed)
+**Input:** outputs=["hello","world"], refs=["hello","world"], 
+         thresholds={exact_match:0.5, toxicity:0.9}
+**Expected:** report.passed=true (both pass), both thresholds show PASS
+
+### Test 5: Multiple Thresholds (Some Fail)
+**Input:** outputs=["hello","world"], refs=["hello","world"],
+         thresholds={exact_match:0.9, toxicity:0.9}
+**Expected:** report.passed=false, exact_match shows PASS, toxicity shows FAIL (if has issues)
+
+### Test 6: Custom Metric (SDK Use Case)
+**Input:** Custom metric with id="custom_metric" in evaluations,
+         thresholds={custom_metric:0.8}
+**Expected:** Threshold entry created, matched against custom metric correctly
+
+### Test 7: Malformed Threshold
+**Input:** --threshold "exact_match-0.5" (missing '=')
+**Expected:** Exit code 2, error message about format
+
+### Test 8: Invalid Threshold Value
+**Input:** --threshold "exact_match=1.5" (outside 0-1 range)
+**Expected:** Exit code 2, error message about value range
+
+### Test 9: Unknown Metric
+**Input:** --threshold "unknown_metric=0.5"
+**Expected:** Exit code 2, error message listing valid metrics
+
+### Test 10: No Threshold (Backward Compatibility)
+**Input:** Normal eval without --threshold
+**Expected:** Exit code 0, report has no "passed" or "thresholds" fields
+
+### Test 11: Threshold Fail CLI Exit
+**Input:** CLI with --threshold exact_match=0.9 on mismatched outputs
+**Expected:** Exit code 1, report still written with thresholds data
+
+## Report Format Verification
+
+### JSON Report Structure
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [ ... ],
+  "passed": boolean,        // Only if thresholds provided
+  "thresholds": [           // Only if thresholds provided
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": 0.5,
+      "passed": false
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### Markdown Report Structure
+- FRAI Evaluation Report (title)
+- Metadata (generatedAt, paths, samples)
+- Metrics section (existing)
+- Thresholds section (new, only if thresholds provided)
+  - Format: "- **exact_match:** PASS (min: 0.9, score: 0.95)"
+  - Format: "- **exact_match:** FAIL (min: 0.9, score: 0.5)"
+  - Format: "- **exact_match:** FAIL (min: 0.9, score: n/a)" (null score)
+
+## SDK Integration Example
+
+```typescript
+import { generateReport, runEvaluations } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = runEvaluations({
+  outputs: [...],
+  references: [...]
+});
+
+const report = generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'refs.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  console.log('Evaluation failed thresholds:');
+  report.thresholds.forEach(t => {
+    console.log(`  ${t.metric}: ${t.passed ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'} (min ${t.min}, got ${t.score ?? 'n/a'})`);
+  });
+}
+```
+
+## Implementation Details Verified
+
+1. **Backward Compatibility:** Code handles missing thresholds gracefully
+   - Check: `if (thresholds && Object.keys(thresholds).length > 0)`
+   - Without thresholds, no `passed` or `thresholds` fields added
+
+2. **Null Score Handling:** Correctly fails thresholds
+   - Check: `const passed = score !== null && score >= minValue`
+   - If score is null, expression short-circuits to false
+
+3. **Custom Metric Support:** SDK users can use any metric ID
+   - Check: Uses metric lookup `evaluations.find((m) => m.id === metricId)`
+   - No hardcoded metric list in core, only in CLI validation
+
+4. **Exit Codes:**
+   - 0: Success (all thresholds pass or no thresholds)
+   - 1: Threshold failure (`report.passed === false`)
+   - 2: Usage error (validation failure in CLI)
+
+5. **Report Writing:** Always writes report, regardless of threshold results
+   - Check: `writeReport` called before exit code check
+   - Thresholds data included in written report
